.\" Man page for go-flow-api.env(5)
.TH GO-FLOW-API.ENV 5 "November 2026" "ETL Madness Flow API 1.3.1" "File Formats and Configuration"
.SH NAME
go-flow-api.env \- environment configuration file for the go-flowAPI service daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
(Linux)
.br
.I /usr/local/etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
(FreeBSD)
.br
.I /opt/flow-api/etc/go-flow-api.env
(macOS)
.br
.I C:\eProgramData\eETL Madness\eFlow API\ego-flow-api.env
(Windows)
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B go-flow-api.env
file defines
.I KEY=VALUE
runtime settings loaded by
.BR go-flowAPI (1)
via
.B \-env\-file
(or
.BR FLOW_API_ENV_FILE )
and by OS service supervisors such as
.BR systemd (1).
.PP
Because this file typically contains database credentials or encryption keys, restrict ownership and permissions to the service account (for example,
.B chmod 0640
owned by
.B root:flowapi
on Unix, or restricted NTFS ACLs under
.I C:\eProgramData\eETL Madness\eFlow API
on Windows).
.SH SYNTAX
.IP \(bu 2
Blank lines and lines starting with
.B #
or
.B ;
are ignored.
.IP \(bu 2
An optional leading
.B export
keyword is accepted.
.IP \(bu 2
Values may be unquoted or enclosed in matching single
.RB ( ' )
or double
.RB ( " )
quotes.
Backslashes inside quoted values are preserved literally so Windows file paths and Active Directory
.I DOMAIN\euser
identities require no extra escaping.
.IP \(bu 2
Variables already non-empty in the process environment take precedence over values in
.BR go-flow-api.env .
.SH VARIABLES
.TP
.B FLOW_API_DSN
Primary database connection string opened at startup.
Supported dialects:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
.B SQL Server / Azure SQL:
.I sqlserver://user:pass@host:1433?database=FLOW_DB&trustServerCertificate=true
.IP \(bu 2
.B SQL Server (Kerberos / Windows Integrated):
.I sqlserver://sqlhost.example.com:1433?database=FLOW_DB&trustServerCertificate=true
.IP \(bu 2
.B PostgreSQL:
.I postgres://user:pass@host:5432/flow_db?sslmode=require
.IP \(bu 2
.B MySQL / MariaDB:
.I mysql://user:pass@tcp(host:3306)/flow_db?parseTime=true
.IP \(bu 2
.B SQLite:
.I sqlite:///var/lib/go-flow-api/flow_api.db
.IP \(bu 2
.B Oracle:
.I oracle://user:pass@host:1521/FREEPDB1
.RE
.TP
.B FLOW_API_ADDR
TCP address and port to bind (default
.BR :8080 ;
falls back to
.BR PORT ).
Use
.B 127.0.0.1:8080
when fronting the daemon with a local TLS reverse proxy (Nginx, Caddy, Apache, HAProxy, or IIS).
.TP
.B FLOW_SECURE_KEY
Default AES-256-GCM passphrase used when encrypting or decrypting artifacts without an explicit per-request key.
.TP
.B FLOW_API_LOG_FILE
Optional file path where
.B go-flowAPI
appends timestamped server logs.
.TP
.B FLOW_API_DEBUG
Set to
.B true
or
.B 1
to enable verbose debug logging.
.TP
.B FLOW_API_STRICT_ACL
Controls strict ACL-only pipeline authorization (default
.BR true ).
When
.BR true ,
all non-admin
.RB ( non- all )
accounts have no pipeline access unless granted via explicit
.B allow
rules in
.IR dbo.flow_pipeline_acl .
Set to
.B false
or
.B 0
to fall back to legacy global RBAC roles for pipelines without ACLs.
.TP
.B FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_USER ", " FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_PASS ", " FLOW_API_BOOTSTRAP_PERM
Optional initial BasicAuth user credentials seeded into
.I dbo.flow_api_users
at startup (default permission:
.BR all ).
Remove from
.B go-flow-api.env
after initial bootstrap.
.TP
.B AD_REALM ", " KRB5_CONFIG ", " KRB5_KTNAME ", " KRB5CCNAME
Optional Kerberos settings on Linux, FreeBSD, and macOS enabling pure-Go
.B gokrb5
Active Directory authentication to Microsoft SQL Server (automatically strips
.B FILE:
prefixes and qualifies short SQL Server SPNs using
.B AD_REALM
or
.IR /etc/krb5.conf ).
.TP
.B FLOW_WINDOWS_USER ", " FLOW_WINDOWS_GROUPS ", " FLOW_WINDOWS_GROUPS_FILE
Optional Active Directory user and group context variables used in container/sidecar deployments for sticky
.I <group>
RBAC evaluation.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
# /etc/go-flow-api/go-flow-api.env
FLOW_API_ADDR=":8080"
FLOW_API_DSN="postgres://flow_api:S3cretPass!@db.internal:5432/flow_db?sslmode=require"
FLOW_SECURE_KEY="prod-vault-injected-passphrase"
FLOW_API_DEBUG="false"
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go-flowAPI (1)
